387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Q3. What is beam search, and how does it differ from greedy decoding?)
/E (Q3. What is beam search, and how does it differ from greedy decoding?)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Ans - Beam search is a search algorithm used during text generation to find the most likely sequence of words. Instead of choosing the single highest-probability word at each step \(as greedy decoding does\), beam search explores multiple possible sequences in parallel, maintaining a set of the top k candidates \(beams\). It balances between finding high-probability sequences and exploring alternative paths. This leads to more coherent and contextually appropriate outputs, especially in long-form text generation tasks.)
/E (Ans - Beam search is a search algorithm used during text generation to find the most likely sequence of words. Instead of choosing the single highest-probability word at each step \(as greedy decoding does\), beam search explores multiple possible sequences in parallel, maintaining a set of the top k candidates \(beams\). It balances between finding high-probability sequences and exploring alternative paths. This leads to more coherent and contextually appropriate outputs, especially in long-form text generation tasks.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
