/E (Discriminative models focus on learning a decision boundary between different classes in the input-output space. They model the conditional probability of outputs given inputs, aiming to accurately classify new examples. An example is a sentiment analysis model, which classifies text as positive, negative, or neutral based on its content.)
/Pg 27 0 R
