/T (Ans - Multi-head attention is an enhancement of single-head attention, allowing a model to attend to information from different representation subspaces simultaneously, focusing on various positions in the data. Instead of using a single attention mechanism, multi-head attention projects the queries, keys, and values into multiple subspaces \(denoted as h times\) through distinct learned linear transformations.)
/E (Ans - Multi-head attention is an enhancement of single-head attention, allowing a model to attend to information from different representation subspaces simultaneously, focusing on various positions in the data. Instead of using a single attention mechanism, multi-head attention projects the queries, keys, and values into multiple subspaces \(denoted as h times\) through distinct learned linear transformations.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1]
>>
