/T (Ans - A hyperparameter is a parameter that is set before the training process begins and influences how the model is trained. It controls aspects of the training process and is chosen by the developer or researcher based on prior knowledge or experimentation. Common examples of hyperparameters include the model's architecture, batch size, regularization strength, and learning rate.)
